### CampusGigs - roteiro de testes manuais
### IntelliJ HTTP Client ou extensao REST Client do VS Code.
### Execute de cima para baixo: as variaveis sao capturadas das respostas.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- CP2
### 1. Cadastrar Ana (com CEP -> dispara a integracao ViaCEP)
# @name registrarAna
POST {{host}}/auth/registrar
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nome": "Ana Souza",
  "email": "ana@campusgigs.com",
  "senha": "senha12345",
  "cep": "01310-100"
}

### 2. Cadastrar Bruno
POST {{host}}/auth/registrar
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nome": "Bruno Lima",
  "email": "bruno@campusgigs.com",
  "senha": "senha12345"
}

### 3. E-mail duplicado -> 409
POST {{host}}/auth/registrar
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nome": "Ana Clone",
  "email": "ana@campusgigs.com",
  "senha": "senha12345"
}

### 4. Validacao de campos -> 400
POST {{host}}/auth/registrar
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nome": "",
  "email": "nao-e-email",
  "senha": "123"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- CP3
### 5. Login da Ana
# @name loginAna
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ana@campusgigs.com",
  "senha": "senha12345"
}

> {% client.global.set("tokenAna", response.body.token); %}

### 6. Login do Bruno
# @name loginBruno
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bruno@campusgigs.com",
  "senha": "senha12345"
}

> {% client.global.set("tokenBruno", response.body.token); %}

### 7. Login do ADMIN (seed da migration V2)
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@campusgigs.com",
  "senha": "admin123"
}

> {% client.global.set("tokenAdmin", response.body.token); %}

### 8. Senha errada -> 401
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ana@campusgigs.com",
  "senha": "errada"
}

### 9. Publicar SEM token -> 401
POST {{host}}/servicos
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "titulo": "Sem token",
  "descricao": "Nao deve passar",
  "categoria": "Geral",
  "preco": 10.00
}

### 10. Publicar com token INVALIDO -> 401
POST {{host}}/servicos
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer token.completamente.invalido

{
  "titulo": "Token falso",
  "descricao": "Nao deve passar",
  "categoria": "Geral",
  "preco": 10.00
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Servicos
### 11. Ana publica um freela -> 201
# @name servicoAna
POST {{host}}/servicos
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAna}}

{
  "titulo": "Monitoria de Java",
  "descricao": "Aulas particulares de POO e Spring Boot",
  "categoria": "Educacao",
  "preco": 80.00
}

> {% client.global.set("servicoAna", response.body.id); %}

### 12. Bruno publica um freela -> 201
# @name servicoBruno
POST {{host}}/servicos
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenBruno}}

{
  "titulo": "Criacao de logo",
  "descricao": "Identidade visual para projetos academicos",
  "categoria": "Design",
  "preco": 150.00
}

> {% client.global.set("servicoBruno", response.body.id); %}

### 13. Listagem publica (sem token)
GET {{host}}/servicos?situacao=ATIVO&page=0&size=10

### 14. Detalhe publico
GET {{host}}/servicos/{{servicoAna}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- CP4
### 15. Bruno tenta EDITAR o servico da Ana -> 403
PUT {{host}}/servicos/{{servicoAna}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenBruno}}

{
  "titulo": "Invadido",
  "descricao": "Nao deveria passar",
  "categoria": "Educacao",
  "preco": 1.00
}

### 16. Ana edita o PROPRIO servico -> 200
PUT {{host}}/servicos/{{servicoAna}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAna}}

{
  "titulo": "Monitoria de Java e Spring",
  "descricao": "Aulas de POO, JPA e Spring Boot",
  "categoria": "Educacao",
  "preco": 95.00
}

### 17. ACESSO NEGADO POR PAPEL - USER na area ADMIN -> 403
GET {{host}}/admin/usuarios
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAna}}

### 18. Mesma rota com ADMIN -> 200
GET {{host}}/admin/usuarios
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Contratacoes
### 19. Ana tenta contratar o PROPRIO servico -> 403
POST {{host}}/contratacoes
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAna}}

{ "servicoId": {{servicoAna}} }

### 20. Bruno contrata o servico da Ana -> 201
# @name contratacao
POST {{host}}/contratacoes
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenBruno}}

{ "servicoId": {{servicoAna}} }

> {% client.global.set("contratacao", response.body.id); %}

### 21. Contratacao duplicada em aberto -> 409
POST {{host}}/contratacoes
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenBruno}}

{ "servicoId": {{servicoAna}} }

### 22. Bruno (contratante) tenta ACEITAR -> 403
PATCH {{host}}/contratacoes/{{contratacao}}/aceitar
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenBruno}}

### 23. Ana (prestadora) aceita -> 200
PATCH {{host}}/contratacoes/{{contratacao}}/aceitar
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAna}}

### 24. Ana conclui -> 200
PATCH {{host}}/contratacoes/{{contratacao}}/concluir
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAna}}

### 25. Cancelar contratacao ja concluida -> 409
PATCH {{host}}/contratacoes/{{contratacao}}/cancelar
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAna}}

### 26. Minhas contratacoes
GET {{host}}/contratacoes/minhas
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenBruno}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Situacao do servico
### 27. Bruno pausa o proprio servico -> 200
PATCH {{host}}/servicos/{{servicoBruno}}/pausar
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenBruno}}

### 28. Ana tenta contratar servico PAUSADO -> 409
POST {{host}}/contratacoes
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAna}}

{ "servicoId": {{servicoBruno}} }

### 29. Ana tenta ENCERRAR servico de terceiro -> 403
PATCH {{host}}/servicos/{{servicoBruno}}/encerrar
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAna}}

### 30. ADMIN encerra servico de terceiro -> 200
PATCH {{host}}/servicos/{{servicoBruno}}/encerrar
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- CP5
### 31. Perfil do usuario autenticado
GET {{host}}/usuarios/me
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAna}}

### 32. Atualizar CEP -> 200 com cidade e UF do ViaCEP
PUT {{host}}/usuarios/me/cep
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAna}}

{ "cep": "20040-020" }

### 33. CEP inexistente -> 400
PUT {{host}}/usuarios/me/cep
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAna}}

{ "cep": "99999999" }

### 34. CEP com formato invalido -> 400 (validacao, nem chega no ViaCEP)
PUT {{host}}/usuarios/me/cep
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAna}}

{ "cep": "123" }

### 35. Recurso inexistente -> 404
GET {{host}}/servicos/99999999
